{
 "schema": "tiles3/details-motifs@1",
 "kind": "top_only",
 "_comment": [
  "MOTIFS for tiles/pipeline/details.py - the maintainer's brief, 2026-09-03: 'a lot of",
  "fun special tiles... rocks, flowers, crystals, small mushrooms, footsteps, cracks",
  "(what I listed is just examples, I want you to think on your own)'.",
  "EVERY MOTIF IS FLAT OR ANKLE-LOW, because that is the line between this domain and",
  "scenery: 'It should be flat or small enough to be considered a ground tile. Larger",
  "objects are scenery... The thing that sticks up has to be small so the player can walk",
  "straight over it.' Nothing here is something a character would walk AROUND - no bushes,",
  "logs, boulders, stumps, signs or saplings. Those belong to scenery/ and asking for one",
  "here would produce a tile the game cannot place.",
  "THE GROUND IS ALWAYS THE MAJORITY. The prompt names the ground twice and the rim once",
  "('X, one small M in the middle, X all around the edge') - the wording measured on the",
  "puddle ladder as the one that keeps all four top sides the tile's own ground, which is",
  "what lets a detail drop onto its ground without a seam.",
  "CENTRED IS CORRECT HERE, unlike a transition tile: a detail is placed ONCE and never",
  "tiled (the wiki reviews it as the centre of a 5x5 of plain ground), so there is no",
  "field to make a polka-dot grid of.",
  "This SUPERSEDES the no-named-features rule in config/tops.json for the detail flavour",
  "only. That rule was right for a density prompt - PixelLab adds cracks and flowers to a",
  "plain ground prompt unasked - but it cannot produce a chosen motif, and a chosen motif",
  "is the whole product here."
 ],
